{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates the probability of the maximum outcome of each lottery. For Lottery A, the maximum outcome is 3000 Euros with 100% probability. For Lottery B, the maximum outcome is 4000 Euros with 80% probability. The reason prefers the lottery with the higher probability of the maximum outcome. Since 100% > 80%, the reason would prefer Lottery A. The relevant information (probabilities of maximum outcomes) is clearly present in the lotteries and can be derived directly from the outcomes and probabilities. Thus, the decision reason is applicable to the decision problem.",
